    {
      "id": "F8",
      "statement": "As indicators, all six alerts look alike: 6 to 8 distinct senders, one transfer per sender, inside one hour. They differ in the relationships recorded after the fan-in. (a) Onward depth: 4 for A-37573, 5 for A-83577, 3 for A-10859, 1 for A-20636 and A-85921, 0 for A-28137. (b) Pass-through completeness: every contribution was passed on for A-37573, A-83577 and A-10859; only some were for A-20636 and A-85921; none were for A-28137. (c) Device sharing on the route: one device on all four sending route accounts (A-37573); one device on two non-adjacent route accounts (A-83577); one device on the first two route accounts (A-10859); none for the other three. The resting accounts with recorded onward reach (A-54215, A-39382, A-92332, A-85287, A-36729, A-10758) have no fan-in alert of their own.",
      "claim_ids": [
        "C-reach-37573",
        "C-reach-83577",
        "C-reach-10859",
        "C-reach-20636",
        "C-reach-85921",
